- Repository tenant-isolation tests for a **TABLE WHOSE *_repository.go + *_repository_invariants_test.go ALREADY EXIST IN THE IMMEDIATELY PRIOR PRD STORY, WHOSE PUBLIC SURFACE IS THE FULL Append + GetByID + ListByOrganization + MarkResolved (state-transition) MATRIX, WHOSE OPTIONAL RESOURCE LEGS ARE NULLABLE COMPOSITE FKs MATCH SIMPLE, AND WHOSE ROW BODY HAS A TENANT-SHARED TEXT COLUMN (e.g. dokploy_resource_id with NO UNIQUE constraint cross-tenant)** (BE-0472 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/drift_finding_repository_tenant_isolation_test.go). Subspecies of the BE-0468 (audit_events) full-surface template with three load-bearing deltas: (a) the public mutation surface is TWO writes (Append + MarkResolved) rather than one (Append), so the tenant-isolation file must add a deepened cross-tenant MarkResolved probe with a MULTI-ROW orgB pool (target + (kind, reason, level)-sharing sibling + already-resolved row) — the existing invariants-file cross-tenant MarkResolved probe targets only one row inline and does not exercise the bystander byte-identity loop. (b) The tenant-shared text shape probe uses dokploy_resource_id (NOT NULL DEFAULT '' with NO UNIQUE cross-tenant) — orgA and orgB seed rows with the SAME dokploy_resource_id value across both Append-bystander-byte-identity AND ListByOrganization-cross-tenant probes. A regression that confused tenants by dokploy_resource_id rather than organization_id would surface as a foreign-tenant row in the list result or a bystander row drift. (c) The optional resource legs (project_id / environment_id / service_id / service_domain_id) are NULLABLE composite FKs MATCH SIMPLE, so the two-tenant fixture seeds per-tenant parent chains (orgA+projA+envA+svcA, orgB+projB+envB+svcB) — a single shared chain would not satisfy the composite FK on the cross-tenant probes, and a missing chain would force every test into the organization-level (every-leg-NULL) shape. The fixture helper seedTwoTenantDriftFindingFixture lands the full per-