stay isolated; this avoids the shared-queue contention that would otherwise turn a per-scenario expectedAttempts assertion into a flake under concurrent goroutines. Forward-applicable to every BE-039x chaos-timeout sibling whose invariant is `client classifies X dependency as typed *yerr.Error with Code=Y under fault Z` (BE-0394 chaos Postgres disconnects, future chaos-network-partition / chaos-rate-limit suites). The fixture-table closed-set member's per-scenario knobs — name, method, expectedAttempts, expectedCode, expectedDependency, call closure — are the reusable shape; the BE-0394 Postgres-disconnect sibling extends this by swapping the fake-Dokploy `TimeoutFault` for a fakepg.DisconnectFault and the typed-client surface for the store layer's pgx pool, keeping every other knob.
